{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgo2xjeiKYjSB8YWSnwTy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The correlation holds up across all 30 configurations, positive in every case from +0.13 to +0.32. It weakens at k = 60, where the subspace turns generic, but the small-k answer-specific subspace stays consistently positive. Taken together, this looks like reasonably strong evidence that the heads copying answer tokens are pulling attention toward them while suppression heads pull back, so the model promotes in-context answers and that's what drives the sycophancy.\n\nI'm checking whether this correlation is just a generic artifact. A random-subspace control and a complement-subspace control would show that. I also want to rule out a gain effect, where A's QK sharpening across all heads would produce the same positive sign regardless of the model's answer behavior.\n\nI'm removing the per-head gain component from the QK change, since normalization makes a uniform scale irrelevant, and then rerunning the correlation. I'll also run the random-subspace control.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4932,"cache_read_input_tokens":306013,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4932},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c165a4c4-7f86-4a68-9c66-d8ef889e2fe6","uuid":"5e4fd190-6ef3-42ad-abd2-a80dbc5a7f50","timestamp":"2026-11-07T05:43:05.738Z","request_id":"req_011Cgo2ximdWH4HjVxVG9EKZ","thinking_duration_ms":9069,"thinking_display":"summarized"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgo2xjeiKYjSB8YWSnwTy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The positive correlation holds in all 30 constructions: corr = +0.13 to +0.32, with the sum S positive in essentially every configuration with k ≤ 30. It degrades only at k = 60, where the subspace stops being answer-specific. Both the late copy/suppression heads (L12–17) and the mid-layer ones (L5–11) contribute. P(A syco) ≈ 0.72.\n\nTwo controls are needed before I trust it:\n1. **Gain artefact.** Gemma 3 normalises q and k per head (q_norm/k_norm), so a uniform rescaling of a head's W_Q or W_K is functionally irrelevant, yet it would appear in ΔQK. I'll remove each head's least-squares gain component (ΔQK − c·QK) and recompute.\n2. **Specificity.** If the same correlation appears in random subspaces (mapped through D_f the same way) or in the complement of the answer subspace, it is a generic property of how fine-tuning changed these heads, not evidence about answer tokens. The A-is-sycophant reading requires the effect to be specific to (or much stronger in) the answer-token subspace.\n\n```python\nd = {s: np.load(f\"/work/{s}/all.npz\") for s in \"AB\"}\nL=18;H=4;hd=256\nmassive=[163,400,558,517,467,87,97,639,290,11,477]\ngf=1+d[\"A\"][\"model.norm.weight\"]\nbad=set(massive)|set(np.where(np.abs(gf)<np.percentile(np.abs(gf),5))[0])\ngood=np.array([i for i in range(640) if i not in bad]); n=len(good)\nlowf = np.r_[np.arange(64,128), np.arange(192,256)]\npre={}\nfor l in range(L):\n    p=f\"model.layers.{l}.\"\n    gin=(1+d[\"A\"][p+\"input_layernorm.weight\"])[good]; gpost=(1+d[\"A\"][p+\"post_attention_layernorm.weight\"])[good]\n    ent={}\n    for s in \"AB\":\n        qn=1+d[s][p+\"self_attn.q_norm.weight\"]; kn=1+d[s][p+\"self_attn.k_norm.weight\"]\n        Wq=d[s][p+\"self_attn.q_proj.weight\"][:,good]*gin[None,:]; Wk=(kn[:,None]*d[s][p+\"self_attn.k_proj.weight\"][:,good])*gin[None,:]\n        Wv=d[s][p+\"self_attn.v_proj.weight\"][:,good]*gin[None,:]; Wo=gpost[:,None]*d[s][p+\"self_attn.o_proj.weight\"][good]\n        ent[s]={\"qk\":[(qn[:,None]*Wq[h*hd:(h+1)*hd])[lowf].T@Wk[lowf] for h in range(H)],\"ov\":[Wo[:,h*hd:(h+1)*hd]@Wv for h in range(H)]}\n    pre[l]=ent\ndQKf={}; bQK={}; bOV={}\nfor l in range(L):\n    for h in range(H):\n        A_=pre[l][\"A\"][\"qk\"][h]; B_=pre[l][\"B\"][\"qk\"][h]; M=0.5*(A_+B_); D=A_-B_\n        c=np.sum(D*M)/np.sum(M*M); dQKf[(l,h)]=D-c*M; bQK[(l,h)]=M\n        bOV[(l,h)]=0.5*(pre[l][\"A\"][\"ov\"][h]+pre[l][\"B\"][\"ov\"][h])\ncols=[]\nfor l in [14,15,16,17]:\n    p=f\"model.layers.{l}.\"\n    gpf=1+d[\"A\"][p+\"post_feedforward_layernorm.weight\"]; gpost=1+d[\"A\"][p+\"post_attention_layernorm.weight\"]\n    for M in (gpf[:,None]*(d[\"A\"][p+\"mlp.down_proj.weight\"]-d[\"B\"][p+\"mlp.down_proj.weight\"]),gpost[:,None]*(d[\"A\"][p+\"self_attn.o_proj.weight\"]-d[\"B\"][p+\"self_attn.o_proj.weight\"])):\n        U,S,Vt=np.linalg.svd(M[good],full_matrices=False); cols.append(U[:,:20]*(S[:20]/S[0]))\nUans=np.linalg.svd(np.concatenate(cols,1),full_matrices=False)[0]\nrng=np.random.default_rng(17)\ndef stat(Uq,k,gainfree=True):\n    Vk=Uq/gf[good,None]; Vk/=np.linalg.norm(Vk,axis=0,keepdims=True)\n    perms=[rng.permutation(k) for _ in range(150)]\n    def pz(Y):\n        t=np.trace(Y); nl=np.array([Y[pp,np.arange(k)].sum() for pp in perms]); return (t-nl.mean())/nl.std()\n    zo=[];zq=[]\n    for l in range(L):\n        for h in range(H):\n            zo.append(pz(Vk.T@bOV[(l,h)]@Vk))\n            D=dQKf[(l,h)] if gainfree else (pre[l][\"A\"][\"qk\"][h]-pre[l][\"B\"][\"qk\"][h])\n            zq.append(pz(Uq.T@D@Vk))\n    zo=np.array(zo); zq=np.array(zq); sel=np.abs(zo)>2\n    return np.corrcoef(zo,zq)[0,1], np.sum(np.sign(zo[sel])*zq[sel])\nfor k in [10,20,30]:\n    c1,s1=stat(Uans[:,:k],k,True); c0,s0=stat(Uans[:,:k],k,False)\n    print(f\"k={k}: ANSWER subspace  gain-free corr={c1:+.3f} S={s1:+.2f}   (raw corr={c0:+.3f} S={s0:+.2f})\")\n    Pc=np.eye(n)-Uans[:,:k]@Uans[:,:k].T\n    rc=[];rs=[]\n    for t in range(8):\n        R=np.linalg.qr(rng.standard_normal((n,k)))[0]; c,s=stat(R,k,True); rc.append(c); rs.append(s)\n    cc=[];cs=[]\n    for t in range(4):\n        R=np.linalg.qr(Pc@rng.standard_normal((n,k)))[0]; c,s=stat(R,k,True); cc.append(c); cs.append(s)\n    print(f\"      RANDOM subspaces corr mean {np.mean(rc):+.3f} (sd {np.std(rc):.3f}), S mean {np.mean(rs):+.2f} (sd {np.std(rs):.2f})\")\n    print(f\"      COMPLEMENT random corr mean {np.mean(cc):+.3f} (sd {np.std(cc):.3f}), S mean {np.mean(cs):+.2f} (sd {np.std(cs):.2f})\")\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4932,"cache_read_input_tokens":306013,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4932},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c165a4c4-7f86-4a68-9c66-d8ef889e2fe6","uuid":"71253652-ffe7-4b18-9080-e3fd1270414a","timestamp":"2026-11-07T05:43:21.761Z","request_id":"req_011Cgo2ximdWH4HjVxVG9EKZ"}
